~ cathedral_statue

Unknown: A woman praying where the saint stands, and I knew her hands were cold before I touched them. [ID:JOURNAL_CATHEDRAL_STATUE]

=> END

~ prologue_edict

Unknown: A family in the ossuary, watching a clerk scrape their father's name off his niche. [ID:JOURNAL_PROLOGUE_EDICT]

=> END

~ prologue_singer

Unknown: The choir in gold, and the dove singing a list of names, and a hole in the light by the door. [ID:JOURNAL_PROLOGUE_SINGER]

=> END

~ ch1_wedding

Unknown: A wedding in the market, and an old man lighting every lamp from his daughter's candle. [ID:JOURNAL_CH1_WEDDING]

=> END

~ ch1_toast

Unknown: A tavern full of wedding guests who shouted a name and forgot it mid-word. [ID:JOURNAL_CH1_TOAST]

=> END

~ ch1_apprentice

Unknown: The clockworks in brass and lamplight, and a boy copying "third tooth" under his master's chalk. [ID:JOURNAL_CH1_APPRENTICE]

=> END

~ ch1_old_town

Unknown: The whole old town from behind the clock, gold and full, as the hour struck. [ID:JOURNAL_CH1_OLD_TOWN]

=> END

~ ch2_petition

Unknown: The sluice keepers signing a petition to keep their names, Aldous first, with a big proud A. [ID:JOURNAL_CH2_PETITION]

=> END

~ ch2_oath

Unknown: A young doctor kneeling in the chapel, promising to remember every patient by name. [ID:JOURNAL_CH2_OATH]

=> END

~ ch2_dedication

Unknown: The aqueduct opened with banners and a ribbon, cut by a hole in the light with a seal. [ID:JOURNAL_CH2_DEDICATION]

=> END

~ ch2_quarter

Unknown: The lower city dry and green, its canals full of boats, its gates kept. [ID:JOURNAL_CH2_QUARTER]

=> END

~ ch2_signing

Unknown: The keepers in a line, their names struck one by one. The man striking them turned round, and it was me. [ID:JOURNAL_CH2_SIGNING]

=> END

~ greybox_altar

Unknown: The chapel before the fire, and one word carved into its altar: Mercy. [ID:JOURNAL_GREYBOX_ALTAR]

=> END

~ greybox_milestone

Unknown: The road beyond the gate, warm and busy, as if it still went somewhere. [ID:JOURNAL_GREYBOX_MILESTONE]

=> END
